            <ArticleTitle>Intermittent anterior divisional block and far advanced right bundle branch block induced by vasospasm during exercise testing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1022-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient is reported in whom exercise induced reversible ischemic left anterior fascicular block and far advanced right bundle branch block. Master's two step exercise test for pre-operative check-up revealed significant ST elevation in leads V1-5, negative U waves in leads V3-5 and fascicular blocks with retrosternal anginal chest pain. Long acting nitrate and nicorandil relieved the fascicular blocks.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
